            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0724" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.51114/4–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-18T17:00:00+02:00">April 18, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 18—2:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1939. I have just received a verbal message from the Foreign Ministry that the
                    French Government has decided to refuse the German proposal regarding French
                    POWs in German custody. According to the official who conveyed this message the
                    decision was taken only after the French Government had studied all aspects of
                    the question. He said that acceptance of the German proposal would tie the hands
                    of the French Government and for the reasons outlined in my 1930 April 18 it is
                    not possible to accept the proposal. He mentioned the fact that despite the
                    decision the French Government is somewhat apprehensive and fears that the
                    Germans may take reprisals against <pb facs="0725" n="715" xml:id="pg715"/> the
                    French POWs. This, he said, was unfortunately a risk which the French Government
                    is obliged to take.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
